# Code comments

When you add or change code, document that code in the same file. Write the comment in English.

Put one line directly above every function, type, constant, and top-level block. Copy this shape: seven slashes, one space, one sentence, one space, seven slashes.

```ts
/////// Say what this code does. ///////
```

Start the sentence with a verb. Mention safety or speed only when that is the reason the code exists.

Shell scripts use the same sentence with seven hash marks on each side:

```sh
####### Uses bun when it is installed, otherwise node, then runs the cli. #######
```

HTML uses one comment:

```html
<!-- Default page shown until / is defined in url.ts. -->
```

Leave these comments in place when you edit the code around them. Update the sentence when the behavior changes.
